text:
## Kol Nidrei Appeal

Donate

### Share Your Support

Temple Beth Israel means many things to each family in our membership. TBI is our spiritual home, our kehilla (community) and our mishpacha (family).

The Kol Nidrei Appeal is TBI’s greatest voluntary contribution opportunity of the year. Your pledge will have a tremendous impact, allowing TBI to continue to thrive and meet the needs of our members. Every gift is appreciated, no matter the amount. Your donation is tax deductible.

Because of you.... Last year, your support allowed us to continue to provide:

- Support for life cycle events from birth through loss of a loved one;

- Meaningful Shabbat services that lift our spirits, like our Friday Night Live, inspire, and provide a loving and meaningful framework for offering thanks to God, or saying the mourner’s kaddish;

- Sunday morning minyans;

- A thriving religious school with 150 learners that makes the learning experience meaningful, provides our children with a joy and pride in being Jewish, and ensures that their b’nai mitzvah is not the end of their Jewish education, but rather an early marker in their lifelong journey as Jews;

- Services and programs to celebrate holidays throughout the year like our Sushi in the Sukkah or Latkes and Vodkas event;

- Adult education classes and speaker series that educate and inspire us as Jews;

- Social action programs like our Rise Against Hunger event which keep us committed to tikkun olam (Repairing the World) and doing deeds of loving kindness;

- And, our very own Chesed Committee, a group of volunteers whose mission is to support our member families in need of assistance.

We hope that this year’s Yom Kippur touches you deeply and moves you to repentance and a new direction in your life. It is our honor praying with you on this holy day.

### Donate
